      "writtenOn": "2023-03-23T08:18:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Have you considered making the right end exclusive? Or perhaps that just makes things confusing?\n\nIt\u0027s sometimes nice that the range 0..20 can be split cleanly into 0..10 and 10..20. That only works when the right endpoint is excluded. Similarly, `lst.split_at(10)` gives you `lst[..10]` and `lst[10..]` by a combination of counting from zero and by how the right endpoint is excluded.\n\nThose kinds of index calculations might not matter much here though since PDL is a somewhat declarative syntax.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 167,
        "startChar": 69,
        "endLine": 167,
        "endChar": 91
      },
      "revId": "5e44f8498a8af1bb04f61fffeb054b379750d882",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
